  {
    "sha": "480017b5682da2785404d56ace14e25c16dd73a2",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDQ4MDAxN2I1NjgyZGEyNzg1NDA0ZDU2YWNlMTRlMjVjMTZkZDczYTI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-15T14:59:09Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-15T14:59:09Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app): a 4-axis wire cut states its stand off and a verify tolerance\n\nThe 4-axis block of a Wire Contour gains two stored values. `widening`\nsays where the wire stands off the profiles: per ruling (the default) or\nuniform. `verify_tolerance` (0..=0.25 mm, default 0) is the chord\ntolerance of the lofted model: the wire verify's kerf law lets a reading\nenter the model's facets by no more than it, and the post gate's report\nstates the tolerance and the deepest reading it let pass.\n\nA kerf gouge now names the deepest reading at any height, and a 4-axis\ngouge with no stated tolerance adds a hint that names the model's chord\ntolerance. The threading and slug laws stay strict.\n\nThe operation page shows \"Stand off\" and \"Verify tolerance\". The 4-axis\ngoldens are regenerated (pose words moved by microns), and the posted\ngate compares its regeneration within 3 counts: the per-ruling wire is\none of several that hold the kerf law.\n\nPinned by wire_verify_tol\n(a_tessellated_loft_posts_under_its_chord_tolerance_and_is_refused_below_it,\nthe_widening_and_the_tolerance_are_stored_and_bounded_at_the_door) and\nwire_four_axis_states_the_stand_off_choice_and_the_verify_tolerance.\n\nFixes #1170\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
